  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 151 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nWe will enjoy more seasonable temperatures in the upper 80s through\nFriday. Over the weekend, the ridge currently over the \nsouthwest CONUS is forecast to begin building east into our \narea. Southerly flow will resume, and WAA will begin warming \nthings up along with compressional warming from the high \npressure. Much above normal 700 mb temperatures will result in \nabove normal surface temperatures, with the Extreme Forecast \nIndex at values of 0.8-0.9. Highs are forecast to warm into the \n90s, and even near 100 F, by early next week. Heat Index values \nwill also rise to 95-105 F, with the greatest values toward the \nMissouri- Arkansas border. These temperatures are as much as 10 \ndegrees above normal for early September. The CPC Heat Index \nforecast shows a 70-90% chance to exceed the 90th percentile \nclimatology range sometime in early September.\n\nRain chances are forecast to be minimal into early next week. \nHowever, rain chances in the extended forecast are persistent \nwithin southwesterly flow just north of our area, which could\nrealistically move south enough to impact central/southern\nMissouri. These chances will be closely monitored.",
